# ELMIR frontend & UI guardrails

Apply these whenever editing UI in this repo (marketing site: Vite, React, Tailwind v4, `motion`).

## Motion

- Use `motion/react` for meaningful motion: section entrances, hover/tap feedback, modals/dialog presence. Prefer restrained curves (e.g. `ease: [0.22, 1, 0.36, 1]`, durations roughly **0.35–0.65s**).
- Respect accessibility: check `useReducedMotion()` where there are loops or large movement; provide static or shorter variants.

## Components — shadcn + 21st.dev

- Prefer adding primitives through **`npm run ui:add`** (shadcn CLI) once `components.json` exists.
- For **21st.dev** (and similar registries): use the **exact install snippet / registry URL** the block provides (often `npx shadcn@latest add "<registry-url>"`). Match imports and paths to this project’s structure.

## UX / visual bar (“premium” discipline)

- **Hierarchy**: one clear focal point per section; readable type scale; breathing room (spacing rhythm), not cramped stacks.
- **Touch / desktop**: interactive controls large enough to hit comfortably; keyboard users get visible **`:focus-visible`** styles.
- **Brand**: reuse **`--elmir-*`** tokens and moss/ivory language from `src/index.css` — avoid muddy neutral greys on green (`white/` opacity tricks read grey on foliage).

## Integration order

- Extend patterns already in `HeroRotator`, `Features`, `AppShowcase`, `Header` before introducing a second animation or component system.
